 {"id":"fabro-fe15","title":"Bake a debug fabro-cli (or shared cargo cache) into the run toolchain image","status":"open","type":"task","priority":2,"createdAt":"2026-09-08T19:52:50.145Z","updatedAt":"2026-09-08T19:52:50.145Z","description":"In the `fabro-toolchain:noble` Dockerfile used for develop run containers (`.fabro/Dockerfile*`), pre-build `fabro-cli` in debug profile or mount a shared cargo cache across run containers so `target/debug/fabro` exists at container start. Evidence: this run's implementer probed `ls target/debug/fabro` and found nothing (seq 107) — the container starts with an empty `target/`, so any run legitimately needing the CLI pays ~7 min of cold build; the workflow graph comment already measures a cold gate at ~15 min worst case. Expected effect: the first cargo invocation in every run drops from minutes to seconds, independent of prompt compliance; complements the config-only smoke cost-tiering for seeds that still need built checks. Distinct from open fabro-cfd6 (prebuilt cargo-chef image for the CI gate, not run containers) and closed fabro-513e (human-facing just recipe). ADR-0019: this finding adds a binary to the agent-reachable toolchain image surface, so it is capability-affecting — implementation awaits explicit user approval. Fix direction stays engine-mediated (image build content / engine-managed cache mount; the prebuilt binary is the repo's own read-write CLI, no new credentials or external clients). Basis: run 01M2183254XQ3HJ45SR4P1Y2X6, workflow version 84429d0a3253eaa52e2406a04a3b97b4365d0ff68b0cdc2f46c296e8c05ec7a6, commit 0dc16012c16ee2f6b2e61ecc73afcf0bd5f26b3d","labels":["needs-user","revision"]}
 {"id":"fabro-e33d","title":"Add closest-match hint to edit_file errors and pin old_string sourcing in implementer prompt","status":"open","type":"task","priority":2,"createdAt":"2026-09-08T20:11:15.657Z","updatedAt":"2026-09-08T20:11:15.657Z","description":"In run 01M219SFJ6A75DS2BP77TBENQZ (seq 92-97) the implementer's first edit_file failed with a bare 'old_string not found in file' because it rebuilt old_string from read_file's line-numbered rendering (reconstructed 4-space indent vs the file's 3-space), burned a cat -A diagnostic round, and journaled a wrong 'transient matcher hiccup' lesson durably. Change: (a) at lib/components/fabro-agent/src/tools.rs:234 include the line number of the closest fuzzy match / first diverging whitespace in the error; (b) add one line to .fabro/workflows/develop/prompts/implementer.md: build old_string from raw sed -n output, never from the line-numbered read_file rendering. Complementary to fabro-645d (scoped reads via sed -n), not superseding it. Effect: removes one diagnostic plus one LLM round per mismatch and prevents false 'transient' conclusions from being recorded as lore. Basis: run 01M219SFJ6A75DS2BP77TBENQZ, workflow version 84429d0a3253eaa52e2406a04a3b97b4365d0ff68b0cdc2f46c296e8c05ec7a6, commit aed06d18be94f10f758651dcaf0eadb97f5d0c17","labels":["revision"]}
